            description: "Fruit Notes reports Fairland as the top yielding replicated strawberry variety in 1952 at Amherst, with 745.25 ounces per plot and 10,305 calculated quarts per acre. Source notes that Fairland and Robinson had been among the four highest yielding varieties over the past three years, and that Fairland helped fill the season where red stele was a problem"
