            description: "Fruit Notes reports Erie at 729.50 ounces per plot and 10,089 calculated quarts per acre in its first replicated test year at Amherst. Source notes attractive berries of fairly good quality, but says Erie was as soft as Howard, had a light colored center, lay mostly on the ground, rotted badly, and was not known to resist red stele"
        },
        {
            type: "Strawberry",
